edgeos-vxlan (0.2.2~rc2+edgeos3.0.1.e50) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release candidate 2 for 0.2.2.
  * Require at least 68 for the VXLAN MTU — the kernel's own minimum for a
    VXLAN device. A value the kernel refuses is now rejected during
    configuration validation instead of after the commit has been applied,
    where the failed commit could leave the active configuration describing an
    interface the kernel never configured.
  * Nothing else changes: the reconciler, the template priorities, the kernel
    modules and the packaging metadata are all untouched.

 -- Vadim Petrov <vadim@vadimpetrov.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:33:15 +0000

edgeos-vxlan (0.2.2~rc1+edgeos3.0.1.e50) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release candidate 1 for 0.2.2: IPv6 VXLAN underlay support.
  * Accept an IPv4 or IPv6 address pair for local-ip/remote-ip, and reject
    mixed-family, malformed and unusable IPv6 endpoints before any mutation.
  * Read the tunnel identity from the kernel's local6/remote6 JSON fields so
    IPv6 tunnels reconcile and stay idempotent across commits.
  * Fail closed when any component of the live state cannot be captured.
  * Restore the previous administrative state when interface deletion fails.
  * Parse the kernel's hexadecimal sysfs interface flags.
  * Normalise VNI, UDP port and overlay addresses before comparing them, and
    reject out-of-range values.
  * Guard every leaf handler with an identity check.

 -- Vadim Petrov <vadim@vadimpetrov.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:43:14 +0000

edgeos-vxlan (0.2.1+edgeos3.0.1.e50) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add native bridge port cost and priority configuration for VXLAN
    interfaces.
  * Preserve configured bridge port cost and priority across VXLAN
    identity recreation and boot restoration.
  * Restore the previous live bridge port cost and priority if VXLAN
    identity recreation fails.

 -- Vadim Petrov <vadim@vadimpetrov.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 17:39:57 +0000

edgeos-vxlan (0.2.0+edgeos3.0.1.e50) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add native EdgeOS bridge integration for VXLAN interfaces.
  * Preserve bridge membership across interface recreation, rollback,
    and boot restoration.
  * Reject simultaneous bridge membership and VXLAN interface addresses.
  * Avoid shell interpolation when applying VXLAN descriptions.
  * Backport the Linux fix for CVE-2022-50405, a VXLAN/UDP tunnel
    socket teardown race, for the EdgeOS 3.0.1 kernel.
  * Preserve and restore the stock EdgeOS udp_tunnel module using
    dpkg-divert with exact hash verification.
  * Document the VXLAN underlay trust model and tested fixed-peer
    firewall guidance.

 -- Vadim Petrov <vadim@vadimpetrov.com>  Sat, 05 Sep 2026 15:36:19 +0000

